# =============================================================================
# Server deployment configuration for Debian 13 (Trixie).
#
# Copy this file to `setup.env` and fill in the values. The numbered scripts
# (00..08) and `run-all.sh` source it. `setup.env` is NOT versioned (it contains
# the database password).
#
#   cp setup.env.example setup.env
#   $EDITOR setup.env
# =============================================================================

# --- Required -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Public domain of the dashboard. WebAuthn (passkeys) REQUIRES HTTPS with a real
# domain: this value feeds WEBAUTHN_RP_ID, WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN, PUBLIC_BASE_URL
# (base of the status page share links) and the Caddy cert.
# It must resolve through DNS (A record) to this VPS's IP BEFORE running 06-caddy.
DOMAIN="orcaster.example.com"

# Email for Let's Encrypt notices (expiry, issuance problems).
ADMIN_EMAIL="ops@example.com"

# --- Database -----------------------------------------------------------------

DB_NAME="orcaster"
DB_USER="orcaster"
# Leave it empty so that 01-postgresql.sh generates a strong password and writes
# it back to this file (idempotent: on reruns it reuses the same one).
DB_PASSWORD=""

# --- Application --------------------------------------------------------------

# System user (no login) that runs the server under systemd.
APP_USER="orcaster"

# Canonical install directory. The repo is synced here and ends up owned by
# APP_USER. It must not be, or contain, the checkout you run the installer from.
INSTALL_DIR="/opt/orcaster"

# Local uvicorn port. It only listens on 127.0.0.1; Caddy does the proxying and TLS.
BIND_PORT="8000"

# uvicorn processes. Rule of thumb: ~1-2 per core. The claim uses SKIP LOCKED, so
# several uvicorn workers share the same DB without trouble.
UVICORN_WORKERS="2"

# Startup timeout of the systemd unit, in seconds (TimeoutStartSec). With
# Type=exec systemd marks the service active as soon as uvicorn execs, so this
# bounds the window UP TO that exec (e.g. a cold `uv run` that resolves/builds
# the venv), NOT the startup migration (which runs afterwards, in FastAPI's
# lifespan). 60 is just enough with an empty uv cache; 120 gives headroom
# without masking a genuinely hung startup.
SERVER_START_TIMEOUT="120"

# Name shown in the passkey prompt when registering/logging in.
WEBAUTHN_RP_NAME="Orcaster"

# Artifact quotas: override of the code defaults for your host's disk: that is
# why they live here and not in the versioned script. There are three different
# limits:
#   - ARTIFACT_MAX_FILE_BYTES: maximum size of ONE file (code default 50 MiB;
#     the setup raises it to 200 MiB and always writes it to server/.env).
#   - ARTIFACT_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES: total per EXECUTION (code default 200 MiB).
#     OPTIONAL: if not declared, the app default applies. A single 200 MiB file
#     already consumes the whole execution quota. See the body limits below.
#   - ARTIFACT_WORKSPACE_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES: AGGREGATE logical quota per workspace
#     (code default 10 GiB). Exceeding it → 507.
# They interact with ARTIFACT_DISK_MIN_FREE_BYTES (floor of free physical disk,
# default 2 GiB): if the sum of per-workspace quotas approaches the disk size,
# the floor cuts with 507 before a real ENOSPC. When raising the workspace
# quota, check that there is headroom against this host's disk.
ARTIFACT_MAX_FILE_BYTES="209715200"
ARTIFACT_WORKSPACE_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES="21474836480"

# Request body limits. The app enforces them (server/.env) and 06-caddy.sh
# repeats them in the Caddyfile, with the same numbers. All four are OPTIONAL:
# leave them commented out to use the defaults below.
#   - MAX_REQUEST_BODY_BYTES: limit for every request (default 4194304 = 4 MiB).
#   - MAX_OUTPUT_BODY_BYTES: limit for POST /v1/tasks/{id}/output (default
#     33554432 = 32 MiB).
#   - ARTIFACT_UPLOAD_OVERHEAD_BYTES: multipart overhead of the artifact
#     upload (default 8388608 = 8 MiB).
#   - ARTIFACT_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES (above): together with ARTIFACT_MAX_FILE_BYTES it
#     sets the limit for POST /v1/tasks/{id}/artifacts: max(TOTAL, FILE) + OVERHEAD
#     (default 200 MiB + 8 MiB = 218103808).
# All are bytes: positive integers made only of digits. "4MB", an empty value or
# a 0 abort (Caddy would read 4MB as 4,000,000 B, not 4 MiB). 03-app-install.sh
# writes the declared ones to server/.env (never a blind default) and 06-caddy.sh
# resolves each value with this precedence: server/.env > setup.env > default.
# After changing them, run 03 and 06 (or run-all.sh).
#MAX_REQUEST_BODY_BYTES="4194304"
#MAX_OUTPUT_BODY_BYTES="33554432"
#ARTIFACT_UPLOAD_OVERHEAD_BYTES="8388608"
#ARTIFACT_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES="209715200"

# Task secret keys: OPTIONAL: if undefined or empty, the feature is disabled
# (the server starts with a WARNING). This is the source of the path: server/.env
# is regenerated on every run. If server/.env already has it and this variable
# does not, or it has a different value, the run stops without writing anything:
# to change the keys file on purpose, set the same new value here and in
# server/.env, after checking that the new file contains the keys that encrypted
# the stored secrets. With equal values it continues. With systemd's
# LoadCredentialEncrypted=, use the form without braces and in single quotes, so
# that $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY arrives literally in server/.env:
#TASK_SECRETS_KEYS_PATH='$CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/task-secrets-keys'

# Extra server/.env variables. List of names, separated by spaces, that
# 03-app-install.sh copies as is from this file to server/.env. It is the only
# channel for server settings the installer does not know about: the installer
# names none of them. Each name must also be declared here (empty counts) and
# cannot be one the installer already writes. Since server/.env is regenerated on
# every run, whatever is not declared here is lost. Example:
#SERVER_ENV_PASSTHROUGH="ARTIFACT_INDICATOR_SUFFIX ARTIFACT_INDICATOR_SYNC_STATUS_PATH"
#ARTIFACT_INDICATOR_SUFFIX=".suffix.json"
#ARTIFACT_INDICATOR_SYNC_STATUS_PATH="/var/lib/orcaster-artifacts/sync_status.json"

# Server plugins. OPTIONAL: if undeclared or empty, the installation is the usual
# one. The real values of each plugin (package, ref, entry point name) are
# documented in the plugin's own README; only examples are given here.
#
# PLUGIN_PACKAGES: space-separated pip requirements, each WITHOUT internal
# spaces. Only these three forms are accepted, all of fixed content:
#   - name@git+https://host/org/repo@<40-hex-sha>  (full commit SHA, lowercase;
#     a tag or a branch can move and is rejected)
#   - name==1.2.3  (exact version)
#   - the absolute path of a wheel (/path/x.whl)
# Rejected, with an error naming the requirement: git+http, a git without a name,
# without a ref or with a branch or tag ref, a name without '==' (or with >=, ~=),
# uv options (items starting with '-'), `name @ url` with spaces, and credentials
# (user@host) or a query string (?token=...) in the URL: a token never goes in
# this file. Write `name@url` without spaces around the first '@' (the PEP 508
# form `name @ url` with spaces is rejected).
# 03-app-install.sh reinstalls them on every run, right after
# `uv sync --frozen` (which is exact and removes every package outside
# server/uv.lock), with the lock's versions as a constraint: if a plugin
# requires another version of a locked dependency, the run aborts. A manual
# `uv sync --frozen` on the host also removes the plugins; to put them back,
# run 03-app-install.sh again. `uv run` (systemd unit, 04, 09) does not remove
# them.
#PLUGIN_PACKAGES="example-plugin@git+https://github.com/example-org/example-plugin@0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567"
#
# PLUGIN_GIT_TOKEN_FILE: only for private git repositories on github.com.
# Absolute path to a file with a read-only token (fine-grained PAT with
# Contents: read on the plugin's repository), on a single line. It must be
# owned by root, with no group or other permissions (chmod 600) and live outside
# the repo and INSTALL_DIR. The installer reads it as root and hands it only to
# git (which fetches the code via GIT_ASKPASS), never to uv or the build
# backends; it does not appear in argv, in repo files or in the output.
#PLUGIN_GIT_TOKEN_FILE="/etc/orcaster/plugin-git-token"
#
# ORCASTER_PLUGINS: server variable (comma-separated list of entry point names
# of the orcaster.plugins group). It reaches server/.env only through
# SERVER_ENV_PASSTHROUGH; if it is declared here without listing it there, 03
# aborts. 03 also aborts if it names a plugin that was not left installed in the
# venv (the server would refuse to start).
#ORCASTER_PLUGINS="example-plugin"
#SERVER_ENV_PASSTHROUGH="ORCASTER_PLUGINS"

# --- Static files that only exist on the host (optional) ----------------------
# HOST_ONLY_STATIC: names (or rsync patterns) of files that the
# operator placed by hand in server/orcaster_server/static/ and that are not in
# git, separated by spaces. 03 excludes them from its rsync --delete (otherwise
# it removes them on every deploy).
# Each entry is a base name: no '/', no '..' and no leading '-'. A versioned file
# with the same name would not be updated either: do not list names from the repo.
#HOST_ONLY_STATIC="robots.txt"
